      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T23:17:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to https://source.android.com/docs/security/features/keystore/implementer-ref#begin_rsa_keys:\n\n\"RSA signing and verification operations need a digest, as do RSA encryption and decryption operations with OAEP padding mode. For those cases, the caller specifies exactly one digest in inParams. If unspecified or specified more than once, the method returns ErrorCode::UNSUPPORTED_DIGEST\"\n\nHere is the case where digest is not specified, shouldn\u0027t the error code be UNSUPPORTED_DIGEST as expected?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1632,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1632,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "2a4bbba944c3564773e903dd36daffa67012ecb3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db5e4625_bd373f09",
        "filename": "keymaster/3.0/vts/functional/keymaster_hidl_hal_test.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1632,
      "author": {
        "id": 1998845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T17:28:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this case conforming to this statement below, please help to clarify. \n\nhttps://source.android.com/docs/security/features/keystore/implementer-ref#begin_rsa_keys\n\n\"Private key operations (KeyPurpose::DECYPT and KeyPurpose::SIGN) need authorization of digest and padding, which means that the key authorizations need to contain the specified values. If not, the method returns ErrorCode::INCOMPATIBLE_DIGEST or ErrorCode::INCOMPATIBLE_PADDING, as appropriate. Public key operations (KeyPurpose::ENCRYPT and KeyPurpose::VERIFY) are permitted with unauthorized digest or padding.\"",
      "parentUuid": "f35b023c_284c2837",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1632,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1632,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "2a4bbba944c3564773e903dd36daffa67012ecb3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fb361a7_4599a75d",
        "filename": "keymaster/3.0/vts/functional/keymaster_hidl_hal_test.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1632,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132849
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-19T19:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding of the documentation is as follows:\n\n1) The first specification paragraph says: \"All RSA key operations specify exactly one padding mode. If not specified, return UNSUPPORTED_DIGEST\". This fits the test case here as it doesn\u0027t specify padding mode.\n\n2) \"Private key operations (KeyPurpose::DECYPT and KeyPurpose::SIGN) need authorization of digest and padding, which means that the key authorizations need to contain the specified values.\" Because of 1), this specification assumes digest and padding are specified and is talking about the value of the digest and padding. Here the padding mode is specified as PaddingMode::RSA_PSS, and if the digest is None it returns INCOMPATIBLE_DIGEST according to the Specification paragraph pasted below. However, there\u0027s no digest specified, and we fall back to the first specification paragraph and return UNSUPPORTED_DIGEST instead.\n\n---\nSpecification for SIGN purpose with RSA_PSS padding and None digest:\n\n\"PaddingMode::RSA_PSS padding requires a digest, which may not be Digest::NONE. If Digest::NONE is specified, the method returns ErrorCode::INCOMPATIBLE_DIGEST. In addition, the size of the RSA key has to be at least 2 + D bytes larger than the output size of the digest, where D is the size of the digest, in bytes. Otherwise the method returns ErrorCode::INCOMPATIBLE_DIGEST. The salt size is D.\"\n\n\n\n\nDoes this helps clarifying it?",
      "parentUuid": "db5e4625_bd373f09",
